n=8:

======================================================================
PROOF: Why 2^(skip-1)?
======================================================================

n=5, flipping arc (5,1) [0-indexed: (4,0)]:
Paths before (transitive): 1
  5 -> 4 -> 3 -> 2 -> 1

Paths after (flip arc 5->1 to 1->5): 9
  1 -> 5 -> 4 -> 3 -> 2 [uses 1->5]
  2 -> 1 -> 5 -> 4 -> 3 [uses 1->5]
  3 -> 1 -> 5 -> 4 -> 2 [uses 1->5]
  3 -> 2 -> 1 -> 5 -> 4 [uses 1->5]
  4 -> 1 -> 5 -> 3 -> 2 [uses 1->5]
  4 -> 2 -> 1 -> 5 -> 3 [uses 1->5]
  4 -> 3 -> 1 -> 5 -> 2 [uses 1->5]
  4 -> 3 -> 2 -> 1 -> 5 [uses 1->5]
  5 -> 4 -> 3 -> 2 -> 1 [old path]

New paths: 8 = 2^(5-1-1) = 8?
Actually: 2^(skip-1) = 2^(4-1) = 8

